  "reason": "PR creation reports and skips PRs opened by bots and stale PRs that already conflict with their own base before checking dependencies.\nFor every remaining PR, shared commits and conflicts from an in-memory merge of overlapping heads require a stack.\nGit execution failures stop creation, and no caller override bypasses the decision.\nMerge commands fetch the verified heads, carry signed assessments only across unchanged diffs and identities, and wait for running checks.\nActive merge queue rules select queue admission, whose eventual result remains bound to the verified heads.\nEvery repository uses the owner's shared gh-stack installation at its pinned version.\nPersisted prose and replies keep one sentence per line in English and Japanese.\nSplit long sentences into shorter ones when a channel limits line length.",
